{"tool_name":"nels","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"nels","home":"https://nels.bioinfo.no","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"Norwegian e-Infrastructure for Life Sciences enables Norwegian life scientists and their international collaborators to store, share, archive, and analyse their omics-scale data. NeLS is developed by ELIXIR Norway and funded by the Research Council of Norway. It can be accessed via a web application, web API, and SSH. Online analysis of data is enabled by integrated instances of Galaxy, including a set of pre-defined workflows.","addition_date":"2018-05-22T19:50:52Z","last_update_date":"2023-08-01T10:18:47.390174Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Web API","Web service","Workbench"],"version":["2018-05-16"],"collections":["CBU tools","ELIXIR-NO","NMBU","NTNU tools","UiB tools","UiO tools","UiT"],"accessibility":"Restricted access","biotools_curie":"biotools:nels","cost":"Free of charge (with restrictions)","credit":[{"email":"support@elixir.no","name":"The Norwegian Bioinformatics Platform (ELIXIR-Norway) Helpdesk","typeEntity":"Consortium","typeRole":["Support"],"url":"https://elixir.no/helpdesk"},{"name":"ELIXIR Norway","typeEntity":"Consortium","typeRole":["Developer","Maintainer","Primary contact","Provider","Support"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["Citation instructions","Command-line options","General","User manual"],"url":"https://nels-docs.readthedocs.io/en/v0.1-beta/"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["ELIXIR-NO","NMBU","NTNU","UiB","UiO","UiT","eca008","matus.kalas@uib.no"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"note":"NeLS enables analysis of life scientific data via integrated instances of Galaxy.","operation":[{"term":"Analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2945"}]},{"note":"NeLS enables storing, sharing, archiving, and analysis of life scientific data.","operation":[{"term":"Data handling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2409"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"NeLS","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-NO","publication":[{"doi":"10.12688/f1000research.15119.1","metadata":{"abstract":"The Norwegian e-Infrastructure for Life Sciences (NeLS) has been developed by ELIXIR Norway to provide its users with a system enabling data storage, sharing, and analysis in a project-oriented fashion. The system is available through easy-to-use web interfaces, including the Galaxy workbench for data analysis and workflow execution. Users confident with a command-line interface and programming may also access it through Secure Shell (SSH) and application programming interfaces (APIs). NeLS has been in production since 2015, with training and support provided by the help desk of ELIXIR Norway. Through collaboration with NorSeq, the national consortium for high-throughput sequencing, an integrated service is offered so that sequencing data generated in a research project is provided to the involved researchers through NeLS. Sensitive data, such as individual genomic sequencing data, are handled using the TSD (Services for Sensitive Data) platform provided by Sigma2 and the University of Oslo. NeLS integrates national e-infrastructure storage and computing resources, and is also integrated with the SEEK platform in order to store large data files produced by experiments described in SEEK. In this article, we outline the architecture of NeLS and discuss possible directions for further development.","authors":[{"name":"Andreetta C."},{"name":"Antony Samy J.K."},{"name":"Azab A."},{"name":"Bongo L.A."},{"name":"Drablos F."},{"name":"Fornous G."},{"name":"Gundersen S."},{"name":"Hjerde E."},{"name":"Hovig E."},{"name":"Jonassen I."},{"name":"Kalas M."},{"name":"Klepper K."},{"name":"Li X."},{"name":"Mulugeta T.D."},{"name":"Nygard S."},{"name":"Petersen K."},{"name":"Raknes I.A."},{"name":"Rye M.B."},{"name":"Tekle K.M."},{"name":"Vage D.I."},{"name":"Willassen N.P."},{"name":"Zhang W."}],"citationCount":4,"date":"2018-01-01T00:00:00Z","j